brief:
I'm Dariusz Wolak, a developer at Bellwether Clinics, and I need a pull request page for pull request 1507 that two reviewers, Esther Mbeki and Colm Fitzgerald, will read printed, at a table, before the 10:00 review meeting on 2026-11-04. The change replaces the yes or no sms_opt_in flag on our appointments with a reminder_channel that can be sms, email or none, so patients can choose email. Sections: "Summary": the new column is added and filled from the old flag in this pull request, and the old column is dropped in a second pull request after 2026-11-17. "The migration": show the code with line numbers:
1 -- step 1, this pull request
2 ALTER TABLE appointments ADD COLUMN reminder_channel TEXT;
3 UPDATE appointments SET reminder_channel = 'sms' WHERE sms_opt_in = TRUE;
4 UPDATE appointments SET reminder_channel = 'none' WHERE sms_opt_in = FALSE;
5 CREATE INDEX idx_appt_reminder ON appointments (reminder_channel);
6 -- step 2, next pull request, after 2026-11-17
7 ALTER TABLE appointments DROP COLUMN sms_opt_in;
"Risks to check": a list: the table has 6.8 million rows and the two updates took 14 minutes on staging, locking writes the whole time; rows where sms_opt_in is empty get no channel at all; and the app code must read both columns until step 2. "Rollout and rollback": run step 1 on 2026-11-08 between 02:00 and 02:30 when clinics are closed; until step 2 ships it can be undone by dropping the new column, but after step 2 it cannot, so the dropped column must be backed up first. Make the point that step 2 cannot be undone stand out.
